                <pb facs="0543" n="449" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg449"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.4112/73: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Schoenfeld</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-06-14T13:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 14, 1924—1
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>304. Embassy’s 212 dated June 13, 11 a.m. If Mexican Government should violate
                    British Legation the Department authorizes you to join with the diplomatic corps
                    in a protest should that body determine upon such action.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
